    "narrative": "For July 24, 2026, the lineup is anchored by **James Wood**, who commands the highest efficiency score of 76.28. Facing a favorable 4.84 xERA in Eduardo Rodriguez, **James Wood** benefits from an elite 0.426 xwOBA and a prime leadoff spot, making him our most reliable engine for runs and power today. **Brice Turang** (72.70) also stands out as an elite play; despite a neutral park, his matchup against the 5.12 xERA of Tomoyuki Sugano provides a significant +19% skill edge, further amplified by his favorable #3 slot. **Tyler Soderstrom** (69.68) remains a high-floor start, capitalizing on the soft matchup against Zebby Matthews to anchor our production at the back end of the outfield.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was sidelining **Mickey Moniak**, who posted a 45.86 efficiency score but ultimately fell short due to a stiff -15% penalty from a poor platoon matchup against Shane Drohan. While **Mickey Moniak** offers necessary speed, the optimizer favored the tactical platoon advantage of **Jose Caballero**, whose 53.79 score persists despite a tough look against Jes\u00fas Luzardo, largely because we must prioritize his stolen base potential in this landscape. We are also closely monitoring **Gabriel Moreno** and **Cole Young**, as both remain \"Lineup Pending.\" While **Cole Young** benefits from a massive +10% order bonus for batting leadoff, **Gabriel Moreno** faces a tighter squeeze against Carson Palmquist (3.45 xERA); if their official lineups shift significantly lower in the order, their efficiency scores\u2014and resulting impact on our daily game caps\u2014may decline. Keep a close watch on weather reports, as any late-breaking delays could jeopardize the expected volume for our heavy hitters like **Austin Riley** and **Josh Naylor**.",
